To delete a given node from the given binary tree
Using recursion
Using queue

If the node to be deleted is the leaf node, then we can directly delete it.
But if it is a root node with child nodes, then we have to find the deepest node (last node) of the tree to replace in its place

Steps:
1) Find the node to be deleted by adding all the elements in a queue. After finding the node, initialise it as keynode.
2) Continue adding all the elements into the queue and store the last node as temp.
3) Then we call the function to find the node with the temp value as it child.
4) Then we make it as null and then make the number to be deleted as the temp.

Code:
void delete(int key){
  if(root.left==null && root.right==null){
    if(root.data==key){
      root=null;
      return;
    }
  }
  Queue<Node> q=new LinkedList<>();
  q.add(root);
  Node temp=null;
  Node keynode=null;
  while(!q.isEmpty()){
    temp=q.poll();
    if(temp.data==key){
      keynode=temp;
    }
    if(temp.left!=null){
      q.add(temp.left);
    }
    if(temp.right!=null){
      q.add(temp.right);
    }
  }
  if(keynode!=null){
    int val=temp.data;
    deleteDeepest(root,temp);
    keynode.data=val;
  }
}

void deleteDeepest(Node root, Node deleteNode){
  Queue<Node> q=new LinkedList<>();
  q.add(root);
  while(!q.isEmpty()){
    Node temp=q.poll();
    if(temp.left!=null){
      if(temp.left==deletenode){
        temp.left=null;
        return;
      }
      else{
        q.add(temp.left;)
      }
    }
    if(temp.right!=null){
      if(temp.right==deletenode){
        temp.right=null;
        return;
      }
      else{
        q.add(temp.right;)
      }
    }
  }
}
